43. Non-Tariff Income.
- 43.1 The amount of Non-Tariff Income relating to the transmission business as approved by the Commission shall be
deducted from the Aggregate Revenue Requirement in determining annual transmission charges of the Transmission
Licensee:
Provided that the Transmission Licensee shall submit full details of its forecast of Non-Tariff Income to the Commission
along with its application for determination of Aggregate Revenue Requirement.
43.2
The Non-Tariff Income shall inter-alia include:
(a)
Income from rent on land or buildings;
(b)
Income from sale of scrap;
(c)
Income from statutory investments;
(d)
Interest on advances to suppliers/contractors;
(e)
Rental from staff quarters;
(f)
Rental from contractors;
(g)
Income from hire charges from contactors and others;
(h)
Income from advertisements, etc.;
(i)
Miscellaneous receipts like parallel operation charges;
(j)
Deferred Income from grant, subsidy, etc., as per Annual Accounts;
(k)
Excess found on physical verification;
(l)
Interest on investments, fixed and call deposits and bank balances;
